<title>FRANCE: French banking commission gets new chief executive.</title>
<headline>French banking commission gets new chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jean-Louis Fort was named on Friday as the new chief executive of France's watchdog banking commission.</p>
<p>He was previously the deputy chief executive, a post he held since 1990.</p>
<p>The Bank of France said in a statement that Finance Minister Jean Arthuis named Fort on the recommendation of Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet.</p>
<p>As the central bank's governor, Trichet is the head of the banking commission.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
